{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-bd939f9344e44dbf", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# MARS: Enabling Autoregressive Models Multi-Token Generation\narXiv: 2604.07023\nAuthors: Ziqi Jin, Lei Wang, Ziwei Luo, Aixin Sun\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_other\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We identify that three of the four gaps between autoregressive and block-masked prediction are eliminable design choices, and closing them is sufficient to recover baseline quality without architectural changes.\n  2. We propose MARS, a lightweight fine-tuning method that teaches an instruction-tuned AR model to optionally predict multiple tokens per forward pass with no architectural changes, no additional parameters, and no quality loss in single-token mode.\n  3. We identify an auxiliary SFT loss on the clean input stream as the key ingredient for preserving autoregressive competence at larger block sizes.\n  4. We develop a block-level KV caching strategy for batch inference that achieves up to 1.71× wall-clock speedup over standard AR with KV cache.", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "372e2c33-5831-490d-9a02-69da930385ec", "uuid": "4b03a595-5549-429e-91a3-836af6e41dd8", "timestamp": "2026-08-14T06:36:21.646Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# MARS: Enabling Autoregressive Models Multi-Token Generation\narXiv: 2604.07023\nAuthors: Ziqi Jin, Lei Wang, Ziwei Luo, Aixin Sun\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_other\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We identify that three of the four gaps between autoregressive and block-masked prediction are eliminable design choices, and closing them is sufficient to recover baseline quality without architectural changes.\n  2. We propose MARS, a lightweight fine-tuning method that teaches an instruction-tuned AR model to optionally predict multiple tokens per forward pass with no architectural changes, no additional parameters, and no quality loss in single-token mode.\n  3. We identify an auxiliary SFT loss on the clean input stream as the key ingredient for preserving autoregressive competence at larger block sizes.\n  4. We develop a block-level KV caching strategy for batch inference that achieves up to 1.71× wall-clock speedup over standard AR with KV cache.", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
